Doug Freyburger wrote:

> I tend to alphabetize somewhat in the order they appear
> in the regular inventory display.

So do I:

Weapon
a  primary weapon

Armour
b  T-shirt     \
c  body armour | these three in a row for easy wearing (b-c-d)
d  cloak       /
e  shield or secondary weapon
f  Feetwear
g  Gloves
h  Headgear

Tools
i  -- misc tool, usually magic whistle
j  Junicorn horn
k  Key
l  bLindfold
m  bag
n  -- misc tool, usually stethoscope or tinning kit
o  lamp
p  Pick-axe

Amulets, rings and luckstone (in that order)
qrst

Emergency items (non-permanent)
uvwxyz

I like not to get too many gaps between letters and move q and further
to gaps higher up until I find something I normally put there. For
example, while I don't have a T-shirt yet, I move, say, my luckstone to
spot b.

I don't like using the CAPITALS; what I don't expect to use soon, I put
in my bag. Anything NOT supposed to be bagged (wands of cancellation,
bags of holding or tricks) are NEVER put in capital spots, but in the
a-z range instead, which I never put in my bag.

An advantage of this is that after a while, all a-z spots are occupied
by things you want to have immediate access to, while A-Z are for items
you collect and once in a while either put in your bag or move to your
stash.

